course: dictionary
lesson: 5251
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look first at the capital letter. «John Locke, an English philosopher of the 1600s, said people make things their own by mixing their work with them.» The capital J shows that John is the name of a person, and the story is about a man who lived long ago.
explain: The same word can also be a different kind of word. In American slang, «the john» with a small j means a toilet. So before you decide what a word means, ask: is it a name, a thing, or a place? Then check that your meaning still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Many people have the same name, so the story tells you which John is meant. «John Harington» designed an early flush toilet in England in 1596. «John Calvin» taught ideas that Presbyterian churches still follow. Same name, different people, and different times.
fact: Names of people start with a capital letter, such as «John».
fact: «John» is one of the most common names in English.
fact: In American slang, «the john» means the toilet, and it is written with a small letter.
fact: «John Doe» is an American phrase for an unknown person, such as someone whose name is not known.
fact: Many kings, saints and famous people are called John, so read the story to find out which one is meant.
exercise: «John Locke was an English philosopher of the 1600s.» What kind of word is John here? | A slang word for a toilet | A type of building | *A name for a person | A place in England
exercise: Why does «John» start with a capital letter in «John Harington designed an early flush toilet»? | Because it is the first word of a book | Because it means toilet | *Because it is the name of a person | Because it is an American word
exercise: In American slang, what does «the john» mean? | *A toilet | A famous philosopher | A saint | A king
test: Which meaning of John is used in «John Calvin taught ideas that Presbyterian churches follow»? | *A person's name | A kind of food | A place to go to the toilet | A type of church
test: What does «John Doe» usually mean in American English? | A famous king | A saint from long ago | A flush toilet | *An unknown person
exam: Which clue shows that John means a person's name? | *A capital J and a story about a person | A small j in a sentence about a bathroom | A word that ends in -ed | A question mark at the end
